{"term":"parasite","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:7ed6d133d062decad6","definition":"An organism that lives on or in another organism of a different species, deriving benefit from living on or in that other organism, while not contributing towards that other organism sufficiently to cover the cost to that other organism.","example":"Lice, fleas, ticks, and mites are widely spread parasites.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":["commensal","mutualist","sometimes symbiote"],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["alloparasite","antiparasite","brood parasite","coproparasite","ecoparasite","ectoparasite","endoparasite","enteroparasite","entomoparasite","epiparasite","exoparasite","haemoparasite","hemiparasite","hemoparasite","holoparasite","hyperparasite","kleptoparasite","macroparasite","mesoparasite","microparasite","multiparasite","mycoparasite","neuroparasite","nonparasite","nosoparasite","parasital","parasitary","parasitation","parasite aircraft","parasitelike"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/parasite#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:97a3668f16a7214905","definition":"A person who lives on other people's efforts or expense and gives little or nothing back.","example":"Of all the corrupting effects of wealth there is none worse than this, that it makes the wealthy (and their parasites) think in some way divine, or at least a lovely character of the mind, what is in truth nothing but their power of luxurious living.","pos":"noun","synonyms":["bloodsucker","bludger","bummer","freeloader","free rider","gadfly","leech","mooch","moocher","parasite","scrounge","scrounger","scunge","smell-feast","sponge","sponger","sucker","trencher mate"],"antonyms":["commensal","mutualist","sometimes symbiote"],"collocations":[],"usage":"derogatory","register":"derogatory","wordFamily":["alloparasite","antiparasite","brood parasite","coproparasite","ecopar